1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A testing walkthrough of ParkinSense PK, a functional monitoring prototype.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The app covers walking, hands, sit-to-stand, reach and grasp, voice, and daily activities.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:32,000
These 3D landmarks come from a real walking recording. They are model estimates, not calibrated clinical measurements.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The hand replay shows measured motion over time. This source does not identify the participant’s diagnosis.

5
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The voice module measures signal activity, pauses and pitch. It does not diagnose Parkinson’s or automatically transcribe speech.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Reports bring measurements and limitations together, with clinician review still required.

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The archived suite passed 463 tests. Wrong-task checks also exposed an important limitation that still needs work.

8
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The next phase is independent measurement validation, patient usability testing and supervised clinic evaluation.

9
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Demo visuals are derived from cited research recordings. No clinical accuracy or treatment claim is made.
